<%# locals: (report:) %>
<%#
  The positions running short.

  A table now that this sits in the full page width rather than a 288px rail --
  what is short, when, how many there are and how many were asked for, lined up
  in columns so the reader compares down them instead of reading each entry.

  Folded by default at both widths. Open, it measured ~500px, which on a phone
  put the first Ranger 2.1 screens down -- the very problem this rework exists
  to fix. The alarm itself never hides: the status band carries the count in
  warning colour at all times, and this is the detail behind it, one tap away.

  Not a width-dependent default, because there is no honest way to write one.
  `open` is an attribute, so CSS can only hide the content below a breakpoint,
  never re-open it -- a phone reader could then never reach the list at all.

  The count says "none" rather than "0": zero is the number a shift lead is
  scanning for, and a word carries it to a reader who is not seeing the colour.
%>
<% have_heading = report.on_duty? ? "On duty" : "Signed up" %>
<div id="shift-lead-below-min" class="mb-4 lg:max-w-3xl">
  <% if report.fully_staffed? %>
    <%= ui_section "Below Minimum", icon: "circle-check", icon_type: :solid,
                   badge: "0", badge_color: :success do %>
      <p class="text-success font-semibold">
        <%= fa_icon "circle-check", :solid, end: 1 %>
        Every position has enough Rangers.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <%# A rich summary controls its own weight -- ui_disclosure only bolds plain
        strings, so the span carries font-semibold itself.

        role=heading on the span, not on the <summary>: ui_section gives every
        section title an aria-level 2 heading, and swapping to a disclosure for
        the shortfall branch alone dropped this page's alarm out of the heading
        outline while the fully-staffed branch below kept its heading. The role
        goes inside the summary so the summary keeps its own button semantics. %>
    <%= ui_disclosure safe_join([fa_icon("triangle-exclamation", :solid, class: "icon-warning", end: 1),
                                 tag.span("#{pluralize(report.below_min.size, "position")} below minimum",
                                          class: "font-semibold", role: "heading", "aria-level": "2")]),
                      variant: :card, class: "mb-4" do %>
      <%= ui_table full_width: true, striped: true, responsive: false do |t| %>
        <%= t.header do %>
          <%= t.heading "Position" %>
          <%= t.heading "Window" %>
          <%= t.heading have_heading, right: true %>
          <%= t.heading "Needed", right: true %>
        <% end %>
        <%= t.body do %>
          <% report.below_min.each do |row| %>
            <%= t.row do %>
              <%= t.row_header row.title %>
              <%= t.cell "#{shift_lead_time(row.begins)} - #{shift_lead_time(row.ends)}" %>
              <%= t.cell right: true do %>
                <% if row.count.zero? %>
                  <span class="font-bold text-error">none</span>
                <% else %>
                  <span class="font-semibold"><%= row.count %></span>
                <% end %>
              <% end %>
              <%= t.cell row.need, right: true %>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
